  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.Kamaraju vs State Of Ap on 6 August, 2019 Honourable Sri Justice D.V.S.S. Somayajulu Criminal Petition No.4625 of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The accused are charged of an offence under Sections 273 IPC Section 54 and 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Section 7 of Cigarettes and Tobacco Act, 2003.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that as far as the offences under Section 273 IPC and Sections 54 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 are concerned, the same are [LEAKAGE_MASK] as they are covered by the decision of a learned single Judge of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, which was followed in other similar cases. With regard to allegation under Section 7 of the COTPA Act, learned counsel submits that Section 7 deals with the sale of tobacco produces without a specified warning including a pictorial warning on the packing. He points out that a reading of the charge sheet, the statements of the witnesses including LWs.3 and 4 does not disclose anything about the \"lack\" of such pictorial warning on the seized material.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that as far as the offences under Section 273 IPC and Sections 54 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 are concerned, the same are [LEAKAGE_MASK] as they are covered by the decision of a learned single Judge of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, which was followed in other similar cases. With regard to allegation under Section 7 of the COTPA Act, learned counsel submits that Section 7 deals with the sale of tobacco produces without a specified warning including a pictorial warning on the packing. He points out that a reading of the charge sheet, the statements of the witnesses including LWs.3 and 4 does not disclose anything about the \"lack\" of such pictorial warning on the seized material.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
